% % The primary barrier is ciphertext expansion and bandwidth explosion. Encoding real numbers into CKKS ciphertexts expands data by approximately five orders of magnitude ($\sim$100,000$\times$). Empirical evaluations of hybrid HE-FL frameworks report up to a 2,000$\times$ increase in client upload bandwidth \cite{he_overhead2025}. In NVIDIA's federated learning benchmarks, full model encryption increased message sizes by 15$\times$ (from 19 MB to 283 MB) and extended the total training time of a SegResNet model by 20\% even on high-bandwidth infrastructure \cite{nvidia2024hefl}. 

% % More critically, server-side computation in iterative HE-FL incurs crushing costs. Deep networks quickly exhaust the multiplicative depth budget of CKKS, necessitating continuous ciphertext bootstrapping. Academic benchmarks place single-iteration CKKS bootstrapping latency at 3 to 40 seconds per operation \cite{ckks_bootstrapping2025}. Consequently, iterative server-side aggregation under HE scales poorly, with some implementations reporting a 15,621$\times$ increase in computational cost per client \cite{he_overhead2025}. For architectures like ResNet-50, running 100 rounds of HE-FL requires terabytes of data transfer and hundreds of hours of computation \cite{fedmlhe2023}, making multi-round HE mathematically and practically untenable.

